// example_attr_naked_non_asm_body.mir — a '@naked' function whose body mixes in an ordinary
// (non-asm) statement. Still compiles (the compiler doesn't know the body is "wrong" in any
// way it can reject outright), but warns: naked functions have no compiler-generated stack
// frame, so ordinary Mirage statements assume something that isn't actually there.
//
// Expected: compilation succeeds with
//   warning: '@naked' function contains a non-'asm' statement; naked functions should contain
//            only inline 'asm' blocks, since the compiler emits no prologue/epilogue for them

@naked
fn f() {
    const x := 1
    asm {
        ret
    }
}

pub fn main() {
}
